 KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGASE TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMMURA SYUZABURO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGASE, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMMURA, SYUZABURO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A small motorcycle carrying an engine which is remodeled by further downsizing an OHV engine suitable for downsizing. A small motorcycle with an engine, which has a head pipe for holding a steering shaft and a body frame (7) joined to the head pipe, and which is provided along the under-side of the body frame (7) with an engine (15) for driving by opening/closing a suction valve and an exhaust valve respectively via a suction push rod (55) and exhaust push rod (56) that are driven by a cam, wherein a single cam shaft (52) for suction/exhaust is provided  in parallel to and above a crank shaft (37) with the crank shaft direction (37) of the engine (15) set in the longitudinal direction of the motorcycle.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un petit motocycle dont le moteur est remodelé en réduisant son volume. Ce petit motocycle comporte un tuyau d'amenée destiné à retenir un arbre de direction et un cadre (7) assemblé au tuyau et est pourvu le long du côté sous-jacent du cadre (7) d'un moteur (15) entraîné par l'ouverture et la fermeture d'un clapet d'aspiration et d'une soupape d'échappement grâce à une tige poussoir (55) d'aspiration et à une tige poussoir (56) d'échappement qui sont entraînées par une came. Un arbre à came (52) unique pour l'aspiration/l'échappement est ménagé parallèlement et au-dessus d'un arbre à vilebrequin (37), la direction (37) de l'arbre à vilebrequin du moteur (15) étant établie dans le sens longitudinal du motocycle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>